0677cc9f-8a76-486f-8b17-e711dda613ec	2026-05-28 11:57:12+00	git	feat: replace single-sim with true multi-simulation graph world architecture	Each disconnected graph component (GRAPH_001, GRAPH_002…) now runs its own\nindependent d3-force-3d simulation in local coordinates. World positions are\ncomputed as sectorOffset + localSimPosition — pure translation, zero coupling.\n\nKey changes:\n- New shared worker src/workers/graphWorld.worker.ts: BFS component detection,\n  one forceSimulation per component with forceCenter(0,0,0), manual setInterval\n  tick loop (d3 internal timer disabled), SECTOR_D=800 >> distanceMax=150 so\n  inter-cluster charge is mathematically zero, cross-component links excluded\n  from all simulations, O(1) nodeWorldIndex for tick-time position lookup,\n  Blue Team nodeGroupIds override with full world teardown + re-seed at α=0.9\n- Rewrite v2 forceLayout.worker.ts with same multi-sim architecture (removes\n  single global sim + custom cluster-center spring approach)\n- Major simplification of GraphScene.tsx (v1): removes all BFS sector hackery,\n  sectorRegistryRef, cluster force useEffect, hadGroupsRef; disables library\n  forces so react-force-graph-3d becomes a pure renderer; worker tick writes\n  fx/fy/fz directly onto d3 internal nodes; clusterCount state drives zoomToFit\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>	episodic	null	\N	0.7000000000000001	[-0.080053955,-0.0486073,-0.03192544,0.00694729,0.07630023,-0.07646115,-0.09706108,-0.012194539,-0.039333344,0.050642904,-0.004544555,-0.027472243,-0.015568056,0.016819062,0.057558168,-0.045124743,0.0698614,-0.05585462,-0.011942326,-0.058072835,0.0034687133,-0.088423744,0.055739947,0.0059204474,0.030458849,-0.027703663,-0.0017995165,0.027298914,0.031088667,0.009392534,0.012296881,0.056555875,-0.044003814,-0.030889008,0.046313573,0.069530584,-0.009591794,-0.022928866,-0.07177648,0.06832787,0.025814656,0.09217974,0.013154258,-0.03810524,0.055134114,0.081970446,-0.09571245,0.0339