332cd7e8-096a-46ee-8f24-71b70e3dd667	2026-05-28 18:08:56+00	git	fix: cache worker positions to defeat library-side d3.nodes() reset	three-forcegraph calls d3ForceLayout.stop().alpha(1).nodes(graphData.nodes)\non every graphData prop change. Since the store does not persist x/y/z onto\nnode objects, d3-force then randomizes positions for any node missing\ncoordinates, wiping the worker's fx/fy/fz pinning roughly twice per second\n(every WebSocket graph_update). Result: every disconnected component\ncollapsed back to origin before the next worker tick could re-pin it.\n\nFix is a positionCacheRef populated by the worker tick handler. mergedData\nruns nodes through pinFromCache, which injects fx/fy/fz/x/y/z onto the\ninput objects themselves so three-forcegraph's d3.nodes(newArray) call\nsees pinned coordinates and respects them. Multi-simulation architecture\nis unchanged — this only closes the leak that was undoing it.\n\nCache is cleared on graph reset, nuke(), and on Blue Team group-signature\nchange so old BFS-sector positions do not anchor nodes after a regrouping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>	episodic	null	\N	0.8	[-0.047380734,-0.083402276,-0.0003676809,0.0056961733,0.041573703,-0.094285525,-0.02489101,-0.051255874,0.0074557643,-0.0003065893,-0.013845705,0.051590692,-0.08273438,-0.00017733719,0.07260545,-0.016884958,-0.004522802,-0.049950954,-0.045087986,-0.0059482926,-0.038388655,-0.08990214,0.049933273,0.025867721,0.03486591,0.028116265,-0.01072534,-0.02888284,0.050362464,-0.035916626,0.038866315,0.024608731,-0.106980465,0.0096782055,0.04581644,0.04783047,-0.023319123,0.00067422976,-0.034065615,0.10140786,0.06632174,0.12887953,-0.03732934,0.026060054,-0.028939549,0.06215656,-0.040766317,8.741716e-05,0.0053499145,-0.023239672,0.023350444,-0.060688,0.020835072,0.06393669,0.0404107,-0.013767359,0.060923327,0.0007451033,0.010052744,0.06277063,0.15453877,0.012227781,0.0621656,-0.05685632,0.065605015,0.040713396,0.047650456,-0.025034247