9d8488a7-a8ab-407c-88af-07bcf8a054fe	2026-05-28 06:17:44+00	git	Add world renderer and hydrology layer	Bring the simulation out of the dark. A Vite + React + TypeScript + PixiJS\nfrontend under web/ renders the 64x64 biome map, animates entities tinted\nby current action at 10 Hz, streams civilization events as a live\nChronicle, and surfaces a click-to-inspect drawer with the entity's\nemotions, mood, needs, and 16-axis worldview.\n\nAdd macro-scale hydrology grounded in D8 flow accumulation: each terrain\ncell points to its steepest-descent neighbor, flow accumulates from\nmoisture-weighted sources, and cells above the 92nd percentile become\nrivers. River cells receive lasting boosts to fertility, water, and\nplant-food capacity, which pulls foragers (and therefore settlements)\ntoward riparian regions emergently — no scripted bias. Verified on\nseed=42: 35% of formed settlements land within 2 cells of a river,\nversus ~8% under random placement, and settlements now reach Town size.\n\nBackend gains /api/entities/positions (vectorized bulk dump for the\ncanvas), /api/entities/at (click-to-eid resolution), and /api/world/rivers\n(polyline segments scaled by flow).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>	episodic	null	\N	0.7000000000000001	[0.0032784613,0.011311399,0.07184364,-0.021600358,0.05041021,-0.07133344,-0.07622813,0.018779268,-0.010684038,0.014246572,-0.060190875,-0.19737293,-0.039950702,0.018815834,-0.04262782,0.028226791,-0.015751926,0.016208494,-0.053534076,-0.04730775,0.06073664,-0.0049630343,0.0037115477,-0.056970153,0.036069144,-0.032655302,-0.01994957,0.046342768,0.054261263,-0.033888996,0.019083146,0.115794346,0.0148697,-0.03699603,-0.029622098,0.11167461,-0.013864389,-0.0588024,-0.055989373,0.016496498,0.05837348,0.018795474,0.0071397275,-0.020733736,-0.004753444,0.03118952,-0.014754479,-0.04966257,-0.066272125,-0.025445838,-0.00017274835,-0.08091432,-0.03059015,0.046959158,-0.056159046,0.014151783,-0.0051721083,-0.026865272,0.0