a3175d2e-5205-4eee-a286-8a88581f8a76	2026-05-31 08:50:36+00	git	feat(tgie): per-session graph isolation (each browser its own graph)	The backend kept ONE global graph shared by all WebSocket clients, so two\nlaptops shared a graph — running a scenario on one showed it on both.\n\nNow every browser gets an isolated session:\n- frontend mints a per-page SESSION_ID, sent as ?session= on the WS and\n  X-Session-Id on every state-changing request (config.ts, App.tsx).\n- ConnectionManager tracks client<->session and can broadcast to a single\n  session; WSBroadcaster gains an optional session param (websocket.py).\n- routes.py keeps a per-session registry, each with its own\n  TransactionGraphManager + active flag; manual submit / clear / get-state are\n  session-scoped, and every build/verdict broadcast targets only that session.\n- main.py parses ?session= on connect and a housekeeping loop prunes the graph\n  of any session whose clients have all disconnected (bounded memory).\n\nClients that send no session id share a "default" session (back-compat).\nVerified: two browsers, run a graph on one → the other stays empty.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>	episodic	null	\N	0.7000000000000001	[-0.05501157,-0.0011282137,-0.055090718,-0.022667298,0.027107224,-0.046206344,0.032759577,0.03752809,0.011853988,0.02377016,-0.012731913,0.05571437,0.00039551876,0.04873418,0.10427688,0.007089862,0.015386,-0.12533426,0.07978918,-0.05292726,-0.010921616,-0.0061425604,-0.0047748974,-0.0081913695,0.011546018,-0.025678417,0.0090317875,-0.027564334,0.04517205,0.03696611,0.01087912,-0.012588393,-0.096786335,-0.034974292,0.025866685,-6.264667e-05,-0.025519071,0.024073837,0.0032399038,0.004356211,0.06000709,0.03101094,-0.0756767,0.033360276,-0.029020349,-0.029709933,-0.08437163,0.05617267,-0.09818798,-0.03488072,0.03716441,0.025501918,-0.047662273,0.08947391,0.0044165608,-0.014789485,-0.009832156,0.04268205,-0.0052032406,0.050367717,-0.011359107,-0.0070927823,-0.01484