a798cb40-9099-4d10-a123-20f7ae68e172	2026-05-29 14:32:44+00	git	fix(graph): decentralized equal-cluster layout + render-loop crash fix	Rework the 3D graph force architecture in GraphScene.tsx so disconnected\nfraud graphs lay out as independent, equally-weighted islands instead of a\nhierarchy with one dominant cluster at the center.\n\n- Remove origin gravity / shared center force. Each connected component now\n  springs toward its OWN evenly-distributed home (van der Corput + golden-angle\n  direction, prefix-stable so adding clusters never reshuffles existing ones;\n  world radius grows with sqrt(clusterCount)). No cluster is privileged at the\n  origin -> balanced "galaxy of islands", no orbital/parent-child structure.\n- Local-only charge for intra-cluster node spacing; links for cohesion; soft\n  overlap-only component separation (actual measured radius) prevents any two\n  clusters from intersecting.\n- Fix permanent black-canvas crash: never call d3ReheatSimulation() before the\n  library has initialized state.layout (it flipped engineRunning=true and the\n  render loop hit state.layout.tick() on undefined, killing the rAF loop). The\n  library already re-energizes on structural graphData changes.\n- Heartbeat-stable mergedData (structural signature) so the 1s WS re-broadcast\n  no longer resets alpha and prevents the layout from cooling.\n- NaN guard + hard maxRadius clamp + continuous debounced zoomToFit so the\n  graph can never drift out of frame or blank.\n- Fix duplicate borderBottom key in TransactionInputPanel.tsx (tsc error).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>	episodic	null	\N	0.8	[-0.047909275,-0.037283655,-0.012603849,0.0005551521,0.060324162,-0.04989665,-0.09914141,0.021731474,-0.05344002,0.04563685,0.021517225,-0.0059079546,0.008554523,0.01973476,0.05400663,-0.0027515362,0.0022561583,-0.040104114,-0.012539481,0.0235091,-0.012077688,-0.066486016,0.0073378785,0.03421947,0.03536465,0.040214043,-0.00014169233,-0.04990824,0.03