ac5fbb57-4427-4009-9baf-acb3fa1d500b	2026-05-28 18:25:55+00	git	fix: stop clearing position cache on group change, add sector debug log	Two changes:\n\n1. Drop the positionCacheRef.clear() that fired whenever the Blue Team group\n   signature changed. It was actively making the bug worse: every fan growth\n   step changes Object.values(nodeGroupIds), so the cache got wiped on every\n   transaction, leaving three-forcegraph free to randomize unpinned nodes\n   back to origin until the next worker tick caught up. The worker's tick\n   handler always overwrites cache entries with the latest world positions,\n   so stale entries between a regrouping and the next tick are harmless —\n   strictly better than no entries.\n\n2. Add a single console.log in the layout worker that fires only when the\n   sector set changes. Lets us verify in DevTools that the worker produced\n   distinct sectors per connected component, without flooding the console.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>	episodic	null	\N	0.8	[0.007491132,-0.03627657,0.02396955,0.0281547,0.0881088,-0.07822727,-0.06004608,-0.10943566,0.019013995,0.017805936,0.028939812,-0.009090542,-0.03408879,-0.048793685,0.020899704,-0.055297725,-0.03126345,-0.060147673,-0.02172288,-0.050495982,-0.08033897,-0.064388745,0.011183812,0.10968672,0.020343123,-0.06773451,-0.014915657,0.03231752,0.045969315,-0.06858499,-0.025559483,0.11691324,-0.042129807,0.021989722,0.06620091,0.07126642,-0.02342695,-0.018374518,-0.04136693,0.041864537,0.035649072,0.07280274,0.03712001,0.013282171,-0.012970176,0.09496849,-0.0029483538,0.0039397334,-0.01304449,0.017549943,0.07199107,-0.021761619,0.08397112,0.008685435,0.022472132,0.022275224,0.07700415,-0.015549962,0.0021063553,-0.021804636,0.13296045,-0.016391065,-0.01004983,-0.095458925,0.013422322,0.0800678,0.04325111,-0.03799717,0.002032275,0.05393972,0.10303203,-0.0066064345,0.018201623,-0.0025726326,0.06825951,0.07596345,-0.09206612,-0.038746234,0.049565695,-0.15830478,-0.01