d36b9833-c95b-4b85-aa67-755ca7b5df60	2026-05-28 10:02:50+00	git	feat: spatial graph separation, browser TTS, and cinematic cluster labels	Voice:\n- Replace ElevenLabs with browser-native SpeechSynthesis (zero latency,\n  no API key). Chrome keep-alive ping included. Remove all ElevenLabs\n  env vars, type declarations, and API calls.\n\nGraph spatial partitioning (v1 + v2):\n- Root cause fix: warmupTicks=250 + d3AlphaDecay=0.10 settled the d3\n  simulation completely before useEffect ever registered the cluster\n  force. Fix: warmupTicks=0, d3AlphaDecay=0.0228, d3VelocityDecay=0.35.\n- BFS connected-component detection with stable compId (lex-min node ID).\n- Per-cluster sector registry: 9 preset grid positions (500-unit spacing)\n  + golden-angle spiral overflow. Sector spacing > distanceMax=120/190\n  guarantees mathematically zero cross-cluster charge interaction.\n- Custom clusterCenterForce (k=0.15) replaces global forceCenter.\n- Custom interClusterRepulsion force (centroid-based O(C²)) prevents\n  cluster drift.\n- New nodes spawn near their assigned sector center, never at origin.\n- Full world reset on graph clear so next graph starts at origin.\n- Cluster label position fix: read from fg.graphData() (d3-internal\n  nodes with live x/y/z) instead of React state which d3 never mutates.\n\nV2 cinematic app:\n- New ClusterLabels component: drei Html anchored to live cluster\n  centroids, showing GRAPH_001/GRAPH_002 with verdict + risk score.\n- CameraRig auto-frames all clusters when a new sector appears.\n- useForceLayout returns {positions, clusters} with sector metadata.\n- maxDistance 600→1400, fog far 800→2000 for multi-cluster worlds.\n- CinematicApp passes blueTeamMultiResult.graphs + nodeToGraphId\n  through to CinematicScene for cluster label rendering.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>	episodic	null	\N	0.8	[-0.061395954,-0.10662517,-0.02803398,-0.011723645,0.054087594,-0.015691375,-0.102906145,-0.021380229,-0.046026874,-0.0