dfb574a1-6e43-429b-87dd-85062715d483	2026-05-31 07:18:01+00	git	feat(tgie): fraud-intelligence copilot, classifier, empty state + graph reset	Turn the assistant into a fraud-analysis copilot and fix graph lifecycle.\n\nFrontend\n- graphClassifier.ts: classify each cluster into one of 12 named laundering\n  patterns with confidence, source/sink, volume, duration, narrative + timeline.\n- fraudIntel.ts: network-wide FraudReport aggregator (exec summary, threat\n  level, pattern mix, breakdown, money-flow story, flagging reasons, top-risk\n  accounts, timeline, AI assessment), memoized.\n- GraphIntelHUD: left per-cluster intelligence card (type, facts, timeline).\n- FraudIntelPanel: right glassmorphic Fraud Intelligence Summary drawer with 8\n  collapsible sections; auto-opens on fraud; accounts hover/click to graph.\n- EmptyState: dormant "no graph loaded" overlay; canvas stays empty on load.\n- ub.ts: investigate_graph intent. App: richer auto-activation narration,\n  Generate Sample / Load Dataset, Fraud Summary header toggle + networks stat.\n- evidence.ts: light professional report theme (navy masthead, white stock),\n  named patterns, real propagated risk, timeline; INR/arrow glyph sanitizing.\n- Graph reset on each run: honor backend reset signal so a new scenario fully\n  replaces the previous one instead of merging (store + App + WSGraphUpdate).\n\nBackend\n- Stop auto-resending the persisted graph: remove connect-time snapshot and the\n  idle periodic rebroadcast, so a fresh visitor opens to an empty canvas.\n- Clear the graph at the start of each manual run and broadcast reset:true, so\n  runs never accumulate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>	episodic	null	\N	0.8	[-0.09391388,-0.02127651,-0.05431343,0.0069647585,0.08795303,-0.0012904862,0.029724574,0.030173343,-0.022985425,0.03215217,0.013930099,-0.037344683,0.05389472,0.028926324,-0.023843087,-0.024696955,0.02274342,-0.067482255,0.027371,-0.0939355,0.02261324,-0.029325787,0.023360